The case on both sides of what a new mayor can actually deliver starts with a

00:07:45.384 --> 00:07:49.464
count in the Vancouver Sun. Two-thirds of the region's 21 mayors are first

00:07:49.464 --> 00:07:54.344
timers, nine of them after beating an incumbent. The fight is over pledges, not a

00:07:54.344 --> 00:07:58.604
vote scheduled for today. A four-year property tax freeze, a police helicopter,

00:07:59.244 --> 00:08:04.084
pools, sky-train. Surrey Mayor Doug McCallum says voters hired the council to act.

00:08:04.464 --> 00:08:08.104
On Monday, a council made up almost entirely of his safe Surrey coalition

00:08:08.104 --> 00:08:11.484
adopted 16 priorities, including that tax freeze,

00:08:11.984 --> 00:08:14.004
sky train expansion, and a police helicopter,

00:08:14.444 --> 00:08:17.524
plus aerial drones for police, four new community pools,

00:08:17.764 --> 00:08:20.644
and an end to some recreation fees and business licenses,

00:08:21.044 --> 00:08:23.424
while property taxes stay frozen for four years.

00:08:23.924 --> 00:08:26.344
He said the people of Surrey did not elect this council

00:08:26.344 --> 00:08:27.164
to study things.

00:08:27.484 --> 00:08:28.964
They elected them to get things done.

00:08:29.544 --> 00:08:31.084
Every campaign commitment, he said,

00:08:31.284 --> 00:08:32.684
is now a council priority.

00:08:33.364 --> 00:08:35.104
Langley Township Mayor Jay Lundgren,

00:08:35.604 --> 00:08:37.104
sworn in on November 2nd,

00:08:37.104 --> 00:08:41.804
said voters asked for change that it is here and that it is here because something had gone wrong

00:08:41.804 --> 00:08:47.464
with how the place was run. Vancouver Mayor Pete Frye, who upset Ken Sim, told a mostly rookie

00:08:47.464 --> 00:08:51.224
council they would do things a little differently and that it might feel like turbulence.

00:08:51.944 --> 00:08:56.964
Surrey Council Harry Baines, the only opposition counselor, questions whether some of those priorities

00:08:56.964 --> 00:09:01.784
are appropriate or even achievable. He said he has not seen a request from the police board for a

00:09:01.784 --> 00:09:06.284
helicopter and that City Hall needs to stay out of the operational management of the Surrey Police

00:09:06.284 --> 00:09:11.344
board. Burnaby Mayor Mike Hurley, back for a third term as an independent facing eight

00:09:11.344 --> 00:09:16.304
party-aligned counselors, said several candidates campaigned on health or education, which

00:09:16.304 --> 00:09:20.864
Victoria or Ottawa actually run. He said Council should not kid themselves that they can

00:09:20.864 --> 00:09:24.324
make big changes there, and that local government needs to stay in its lane.

00:09:25.004 --> 00:09:31.044
Daryl Masado, North Vancouver City Mayor from 2005 to 2018, said the job is much harder

00:09:31.044 --> 00:09:34.644
than it looks, and that big promises are easy to make and harder to keep.

00:09:34.644 --> 00:09:40.624
New Westminster Mayor Daniel Fontaine, who unceded an incumbent, said cities collect just pennies

00:09:40.624 --> 00:09:45.984
of every tax dollar, so the money for major work is limited. His council did pass a 100-day

00:09:45.984 --> 00:09:51.704
plan for more garbage bins, sidewalk repairs, easier traffic bottlenecks, and an end-to-restaurant

00:09:51.704 --> 00:09:57.224
